      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is the unfreeze after having frozen @ line 3009 because of the `false` argument here. I could make a named function for unfreeze (`unfreezePackageCgroup()`) to make this more clear. Yes/no?\n\nBut I think you may be correct about unnecessarily freezing dependent cgroups during the kills for dependent packages. (Summary here: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1Z3lF_-RxMWHAKwXSiCNhAKHuT3sEIEVbMTvQ6VdARdQ/edit#slide\u003did.g13c0afefd05_0_2) Where package_A\u0027s UID !\u003d package_B\u0027s UID, here we would freeze all of package_B and then unfreeze it, blocking potentially unrelated processes during the time we\u0027re killing as subset of processes in package_B.\n\nSo we want to skip cgroup freezes and unfreezes for dependent processes; could we check `proc.first.getPkgDeps().contains(packageName)` and skip freezes when that\u0027s true, since we know we\u0027re killing a dependent process in that case?",
